(Source: Sports Medicine & Environmental Health Institute) Tj T*
(Topic: Athletic Training, Exercise, and Outdoor Activity Safety) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Exercise Risk Matrix:) Tj T*
(1. Ventilation Rate Impact: Strenuous exercise increases inhalation of ambient pollutants by 4x to 8x.) Tj T*
(2. AQI <= 50: All outdoor physical activities, running, and competitive sports safe.) Tj T*
(3. AQI 51-100: Safe for healthy athletes. Monitor athletes with asthma or exercise-induced bronchospasm.) Tj T*
(4. AQI 101-150: Reduce duration and intensity of outdoor workouts. Substitute high-intensity cardio with indoor training.) Tj T*
(5. AQI > 150: Cancel or move all outdoor endurance sports and school athletic practices indoors.) Tj T*
(6. Timing Optimization: Avoid training near major highways during 07:00-09:00 and 17:00-19:00 peak traffic hours.) Tj T*
